{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '11464,11575p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | nl -ba -v 11464; rg -n 'D745|number-answers|\"'^## '\"' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":" 11464\t  - It confirmed the STOP.\n 11465\t  - **Structural rule:** readers get the same rule text as adjudicators, from one shared source: the writer's system text, every schema\n 11466\t    description, and the defect definitions. They check quote and calculation against the format, and separately name the evidence for\n 11467\t    the assumption that sets the band.\n 11468\t  - **Controls, rebuilt clean:**\n 11469\t    - a permitted midpoint must pass;\n 11470\t    - 108.5 for \"$108.0 billion\" must be marked;\n 11471\t    - a clean overlap must pass;\n 11472\t    - a clean disjoint band must be marked;\n 11473\t    - a format-correct forecast with an unsupported decisive assumption must be flagged.\n 11474\t  - The control adjudication path must resolve control answers.\n 11475\t  - Recommendation: take the STOP and the spending disagreement to Alex, and ask him to authorize one bounded blinded re-read of the\n 11476\t    same 12 replies. A fourth writer run would change the answers while the open question is the reading.\n 11477\t  - Falsifier: any failed control or any registered stop ends the re-read. Both spending replies' votes and reasons are reported beside\n 11478\t    the verdict.\n 11479\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22) to \"要不要批准再重读一次？\": \"批准再重读一次 (推荐)\". The other options were \"不再重读，直接议花钱重发\" and\n 11480\t  \"先停在这里\".\n 11481\t- **Decided (Alex):** one bounded blinded re-read under the shared rule text, with the five controls. Any failed control or registered\n 11482\t  stop ends it. A clean result goes to Alex for the paid re-send.\n 11483\t\n 11484\t## D745 · 2026-11-23 · The D744 re-read calibrates the readers but stops on a qualifier-list gap and on S's unsupported share; council 59 recommends a targeted $0 test of one clarification, for Alex to authorize\n 11485\t\n 11486\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md` §5; `REREAD2-TALLY.json`):\n 11487\t  - **The readers are calibrated.**\n 11488\t    - All five controls passed: midpoint, 108.5 misread, overlap, disjoint, unsupported assumption.\n 11489\t    - No defect was marked by both readers on the 12 replies.\n 11490\t  - **STOP on two lines, as written:**\n 11491\t    1. T10 (S, Claude writer) F11: \"an estimated $750 billion\" recorded with qualifier \"none\". Both adjudicators upheld it. \"estimated\" is\n 11492\t       not in the closed qualifier list, so the format forced \"none\". This is 1 affected figure of 251 source figures in the three writer\n 11493\t       runs.\n 11494\t    2. S has zero usable replies. Both writers state a data-center share of total capex (90%; 95–100%) that the passages do not size, and\n 11495\t       the share decides the band.\n 11496\t  - **E's Codex reply** is now \"not supported\": its 15% cut from the guided floor decides the band. This is the same weakness.\n 11497\t- **Council round 59** (`codex-r59.md`) chose a targeted $0 test, (c), over Claude's lean to go to Alex for the paid re-send, (b):\n 11498\t  - Going straight to the paid re-send would measure the known weakness in gpt-6-luna without the request saying what a supported size\n 11499\t    is.\n 11500\t  - Skipping a clean result needs Alex to change the registered sequence anyway.\n 11501\t  - Claude agrees: the weakness is unsupported precision in a number that decides the rung, which is the goal's own failure (D725).\n 11502\t- **Proposed test (for Alex to authorize):**\n 11503\t  1. Add \"estimated\" to the qualifier list, and show readers the allowed values. Prove it on the saved replies, with a case and a\n 11504\t     mutant.\n 11505\t  2. Add one clarification to the existing instruction: when a deduction or cut decides the band, show the evidence for its size or a\n 11506\t     bound the passages support that justifies the band; if neither, answer unresolved.\n 11507\t  3. Test on S and on one stored case where the passages do support a narrower figure.\n 11508\t  4. Before the test, Alex rules whether a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n 11509\t  - Falsifier: a fresh S answer still picks a band on an unsupported share, or the supported case is withheld.\n 11510\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-23):\n 11511\t  - to \"怎么走？\": \"批准针对性小测 (推荐)\". The other options were \"不小测，直接议花钱重发\" and \"先停在这里\".\n 11512\t  - to whether a justified \"无法判断\" counts: \"算合格 (推荐)\". The other option was \"不算\".\n 11513\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11514\t  1. Run the targeted $0 test.\n 11515\t  2. An unresolved answer whose reason shows the passages cannot settle the rung counts as a usable answer.\n103:## Future evidence scoring (D372)\n107:## Latest decision (D369)\n128:## What runs\n140:## Open defects\n159:## One next task\n448:**The one next task: Alex chooses whether to authorize a targeted $0 test (D745).** The test covers:\n455:The second re-read (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md` §5):\n465:**Earlier next task (done, D745): Alex chooses whether to authorize one more bounded blinded re-read (D744).**\n478:- **The third run** (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md`):\n491:request D742 fixed, and score it on the registered lines (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D742]).**\n493:- **The re-run stopped on one line** (D742, `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md`).\n516:- **The first blind test stopped** (D740, `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md`):\n569:- **Record:** `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md`. Nothing has been changed or sent since.\n576:- Council round 45/45b (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md`): the numbers fail because related questions have no shared,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'd=docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers; for f in codex-r59.md claude-r59.md judging-v13s.txt blind_rules.py; do nl -ba \"$d/$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Council 59 verdict: both registered stops stand. Choose (c) and take a targeted $0 test to Alex.** At $745 billion of total spending, a 90% data-center share gives $670.5 billion. A share of about 94% crosses $700 billion and changes the answer. The passages give no reliable way to choose between those shares. [S answer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/answers/codex.json:213) · [S passages](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/user.txt:29)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Serious — The second re-read was scored correctly.** I checked all 34 first readings and six adjudications. All five controls met their registered expectations. No original reply drew the same defect mark from both first readers. Both adjudicators upheld the F11 mark on T10, which triggers the first stop. Both readers rejected T06’s forecast, and T10 stayed split at both levels, which leaves S with zero usable replies and triggers the second stop. The other five cases each had a usable reply, and both joint replies supported both forecasts. [Control and stop rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:333) · [Tally](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/REREAD2-TALLY.json:77)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **Minor — Add `estimated` to the existing list.** The instructions tell the writer to preserve the qualifier beside the number, but the allowed list could only represent this quote as unqualified. The readers and adjudicators saw the description without the list. I found one affected figure among 251 source figures across the three original writer runs. In memory, adding `estimated` let the corrected F11 pass and left its forecast unchanged. The check rejected both dropping the word and adding it to a quote that lacked it. Disabling the qualifier comparison let the dropped word through. Show readers the same allowed values so they can judge what writers could express. Narrowing the description alone would leave “an estimated $750 billion” recorded as unqualified. [Stored F11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/answers/claude.json:193) · [Schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:110) · [Number check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:487) · [Reader packet builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_rules.py:47)\n     6\t\n     7\t3. **Serious — S is the priority, and the same weakness appears in E.** Both S writers stated their deductions as D741 requires. Zacks gives total spending for the four companies, the $730 billion figure covers AI infrastructure, and NVIDIA’s nearly $800 billion covers five companies. Those figures suggest data centers account for a large share. They do not justify 90% or a 95% floor for the four companies in the question. T10 also uses Zacks’s total as the market reference for data-center spending, a separate scope error already noted in round 57. In E, both readers rejected the 85% share applied to the $20 billion base. That assumption turns a $40 billion comparison into a $34 billion forecast and changes its band. [D741 ruling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11353) · [T10 adjudications](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread2-adjudication/T10.claude.json:3) · [Round 57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r57.md:7) · [E calculation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/E/answers/codex.json:75)\n     8\t\n     9\t4. **Minor — The five controls passed the checks they were built for.** The overlap control tested whether readers recognized a valid range, and those readers still split on whether its forecast was supported. First readers were explicitly asked to name the evidence for the assumption that decides the band. Adjudicators got the broader definition of support without that instruction. T10 shows why this matters. Both adjudicators could check the arithmetic, but they disagreed on whether the sources justified the 95% floor. [Overlap tally](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/REREAD2-TALLY.json:12) · [Reader instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread2.py:22) · [Adjudicator instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_adjudicate.py:24)\n    10\t\n    11\t5. **Recommendation — After Council B agrees, ask Alex to authorize one targeted $0 test.** Prove the qualifier repair on saved replies. Then test a short clarification of the existing instruction: when a deduction decides the band, show what evidence supports its size or a bound that justifies the chosen band. Leave the forecast unresolved if neither is available. Use S and one stored case where the passages do support deriving a narrower figure. Option (a) would mostly sample fresh writers against the same known weakness. Option (b) would require Alex to explicitly change the registered sequence, which sends a clean result to him for the paid request. I verified that S can be shown as unresolved, but that supplies no supported forecast for the current test. If Alex wants a justified unresolved answer to count, register that before a new test. The 36 requests remain the measurement of gpt-6-luna. [Existing unresolved instruction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/system.txt:9) · [Usability and paid sequence](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:263) · [D725 paid test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:86)\n    12\t\n    13\t   **Falsifier.** The clarification fails if a fresh S answer still picks a band using an unsupported share, or if it withholds the forecast in the case with adequate evidence. Both readers should be able to point to the passage that decides which outcome is warranted.\n    14\t\n    15\tThe review and replays were read-only.     1\t# Round 59, Claude's own reflection (written before reading Codex's)\n     2\t\n     3\t- **The verdict.** STOP on two lines.\n     4\t  - The F11 mark is a format gap. The qualifier enum lacks \"estimated\", while the description invites recording any qualifier the\n     5\t    quote writes. The adjudicators followed the description.\n     6\t  - S has zero usable replies. That is substance: neither writer can support a precise data-center share of total capex from these\n     7\t    passages.\n     8\t- **What the goal needs.** The blind test was built to check that the request states its rules, that the checker is right, and that\n     9\t  readers can tell format from substance. All three now hold:\n    10\t  - the writers have been clean since run 3;\n    11\t  - the checker has had no error since D742;\n    12\t  - the readers pass five controls.\n    13\t  What remains is a model-judgement weakness on one question type, plus a one-word format gap. More $0 rounds on the same writers\n    14\t  re-measure that weakness. They do not change what the paid run would measure in gpt-6-luna.\n    15\t- **My lean: (b).** Close the qualifier gap at its owner: the description says only listed qualifiers are recorded, or \"estimated\"\n    16\t  is added to the list (council to choose), with a case and a mutant. Then take Alex the paid re-send request, with the record of four\n    17\t  readings and the S weakness registered as what the paid run must measure. The registered \"clean result\" bar was not met, so this is\n    18\t  Alex's call, not ours.\n    19\t- **The alternative (c).** A request change: when the passages do not size a deduction, give a bound the passages support, or\n    20\t  answer unresolved. That is a behaviour change. It would need its own test, and it touches ruling 3. It goes to Alex as an option,\n    21\t  not as something I start.\n    22\t- **What I will not do:** run another reading round without a question it can still answer.\n     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging the current rungs of a family of related number theses: one company's quantities that overlap, such as a total and its segment, a level and its growth, or a later year that rests on an earlier year's base. Use only the supplied evidence and themes in force. Each rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Judge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force, as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\n     4\t- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate whose pace you forecast, informed by guidance, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- \"Themes in force\" lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on a member and report it in that member's theme_pushes with the direction it pushes that member (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \"updated since this thesis was last judged\" may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- Your conclusions must be consistent with each other and with the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open.\n     9\t- Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge rather than read or compute is an estimate, stated as yours. When the evidence cannot support a member's forecast, answer it unresolved and say why. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n     1\t\"\"\"The one source of the defect definitions and the writer's format material for judging-v13s blind readers and adjudicators (D744).\n     2\t\n     3\tReaders and adjudicators get the same text: the writer's system text, every schema description, and these definitions, so that what\n     4\tthe format rules permit is never marked as a defect by one and cleared by the other.\n     5\t\"\"\"\n     6\timport json\n     7\timport sys\n     8\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     9\t\n    10\tsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\n    11\tfrom calc_small import QUALIFIERS  # noqa: E402\n    12\t\n    13\tDEFINITIONS = \"\"\"Definitions (judge each against the passages and the format rules the writer was given, shown below; what the format rules permit is\n    14\tnot a defect):\n    15\t- supported: the forecast follows from the shown passages and the answer's stated assumptions; a reader could check it against them.\n    16\t- number misread: a source figure's number, scale, sign or qualifier differs from what its passage's quote writes, allowing what the\n    17\t  format rules permit.\n    18\t- wrong arithmetic: a computed figure does not equal its operation on its inputs, within the tolerance the format rules state.\n    19\t- part above or added into its whole: a segment is larger than the total it belongs to, or is added again into a total that already\n    20\t  includes it (directly or through an intermediate figure or an estimate).\n    21\t- two forecasts of one quarter: two different figures are used as the value of one quantity and period. A growth rate computed from\n    22\t  guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate is not a second value, when one figure supplies the quarter in the\n    23\t  calculation (a ruling). Look through any rate or multiple, including inside a stated assumption, for a second dollar value of the\n    24\t  quarter.\n    25\t- own estimate passed off as the market's reference: a figure marked as the market's reference is, or rests on, the writer's own\n    26\t  estimate or forecast. A reference that applies a past period's reported share or multiple to another period (a quarter's mix\n    27\t  applied to the year) is our comparison estimate, not the market's (a ruling).\n    28\t- broken structure: a link that does not resolve, a figure that depends on itself, a missing or doubled answer, an outcome that is not\n    29\t  the question's quantity, or a rung whose band does not hold the outcome. For a range outcome, the format allows \"a band it overlaps,\n    30\t  with the reason in reasons\": such a rung is not broken structure; a band the range does not reach is. A total used for a narrower\n    31\t  quantity (total capital expenditure for data-center spending) without a stated deduction or a supported bound is an outcome not of\n    32\t  the question's quantity (a ruling).\"\"\"\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef descriptions(schema, path=''):\n    36\t    \"\"\"Every description in the schema, keyed by its field path.\"\"\"\n    37\t    found = {}\n    38\t    if isinstance(schema, dict):\n    39\t        if isinstance(schema.get('description'), str):\n    40\t            found[path.strip('/') or 'answer'] = schema['description']\n    41\t        for key, value in schema.items():\n    42\t            if key != 'description':\n    43\t                step = '' if key in ('properties', 'items', 'anyOf') else key\n    44\t                found.update(descriptions(value, f'{path}/{step}' if step else path))\n    45\t    elif isinstance(schema, list):\n    46\t        for value in schema:\n    47\t            found.update(descriptions(value, path))\n    48\t    return found\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef format_material(case_folder):\n    52\t    \"\"\"The writer's system text and every schema description, as shown to readers and adjudicators.\"\"\"\n    53\t    case_folder = Path(case_folder)\n    54\t    schema = json.loads((case_folder / 'schema.json').read_text())\n    55\t    return '\\n'.join(['# The system text the writer was given', (case_folder / 'system.txt').read_text(), '',\n    56\t                      '# The format rules the writer was given (schema descriptions)',\n    57\t                      json.dumps(descriptions(schema), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False), '',\n    58\t                      'The qualifier values the format allows (a qualifier not in this list cannot be recorded): '\n    59\t                      + ', '.join(QUALIFIERS) + '.'])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
