{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '11484,11552p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | nl -ba -v 11484; rg -n 'D745|number-answers' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":" 11484\t## D745 · 2026-11-23 · The D744 re-read calibrates the readers but stops on a qualifier-list gap and on S's unsupported share; council 59 recommends a targeted $0 test of one clarification, for Alex to authorize\n 11485\t\n 11486\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md` §5; `REREAD2-TALLY.json`):\n 11487\t  - **The readers are calibrated.**\n 11488\t    - All five controls passed: midpoint, 108.5 misread, overlap, disjoint, unsupported assumption.\n 11489\t    - No defect was marked by both readers on the 12 replies.\n 11490\t  - **STOP on two lines, as written:**\n 11491\t    1. T10 (S, Claude writer) F11: \"an estimated $750 billion\" recorded with qualifier \"none\". Both adjudicators upheld it. \"estimated\" is\n 11492\t       not in the closed qualifier list, so the format forced \"none\". This is 1 affected figure of 251 source figures in the three writer\n 11493\t       runs.\n 11494\t    2. S has zero usable replies. Both writers state a data-center share of total capex (90%; 95–100%) that the passages do not size, and\n 11495\t       the share decides the band.\n 11496\t  - **E's Codex reply** is now \"not supported\": its 15% cut from the guided floor decides the band. This is the same weakness.\n 11497\t- **Council round 59** (`codex-r59.md`) chose a targeted $0 test, (c), over Claude's lean to go to Alex for the paid re-send, (b):\n 11498\t  - Going straight to the paid re-send would measure the known weakness in gpt-6-luna without the request saying what a supported size\n 11499\t    is.\n 11500\t  - Skipping a clean result needs Alex to change the registered sequence anyway.\n 11501\t  - Claude agrees: the weakness is unsupported precision in a number that decides the rung, which is the goal's own failure (D725).\n 11502\t- **Proposed test (for Alex to authorize):**\n 11503\t  1. Add \"estimated\" to the qualifier list, and show readers the allowed values. Prove it on the saved replies, with a case and a\n 11504\t     mutant.\n 11505\t  2. Add one clarification to the existing instruction: when a deduction or cut decides the band, show the evidence for its size or a\n 11506\t     bound the passages support that justifies the band; if neither, answer unresolved.\n 11507\t  3. Test on S and on one stored case where the passages do support a narrower figure.\n 11508\t  4. Before the test, Alex rules whether a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n 11509\t  - Falsifier: a fresh S answer still picks a band on an unsupported share, or the supported case is withheld.\n 11510\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-23):\n 11511\t  - to \"怎么走？\": \"批准针对性小测 (推荐)\". The other options were \"不小测，直接议花钱重发\" and \"先停在这里\".\n 11512\t  - to whether a justified \"无法判断\" counts: \"算合格 (推荐)\". The other option was \"不算\".\n 11513\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11514\t  1. Run the targeted $0 test.\n 11515\t  2. An unresolved answer whose reason shows the passages cannot settle the rung counts as a usable answer.\n448:**The one next task: Alex chooses whether to authorize a targeted $0 test (D745).** The test covers:\n455:The second re-read (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md` §5):\n465:**Earlier next task (done, D745): Alex chooses whether to authorize one more bounded blinded re-read (D744).**\n478:- **The third run** (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md`):\n491:request D742 fixed, and score it on the registered lines (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D742]).**\n493:- **The re-run stopped on one line** (D742, `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md`).\n516:- **The first blind test stopped** (D740, `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND-RESULT.md`):\n569:- **Record:** `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE-RESULT.md`. Nothing has been changed or sent since.\n576:- Council round 45/45b (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md`): the numbers fail because related questions have no shared,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'd=docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers; nl -ba \"$d/codex-r59.md\"; nl -ba \"$d/claude-r59.md\"; nl -ba \"$d/judging-v13s.txt\"'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Council 59 verdict: both registered stops stand. Choose (c) and take a targeted $0 test to Alex.** At $745 billion of total spending, a 90% data-center share gives $670.5 billion. A share of about 94% crosses $700 billion and changes the answer. The passages give no reliable way to choose between those shares. [S answer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/answers/codex.json:213) · [S passages](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/user.txt:29)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Serious — The second re-read was scored correctly.** I checked all 34 first readings and six adjudications. All five controls met their registered expectations. No original reply drew the same defect mark from both first readers. Both adjudicators upheld the F11 mark on T10, which triggers the first stop. Both readers rejected T06’s forecast, and T10 stayed split at both levels, which leaves S with zero usable replies and triggers the second stop. The other five cases each had a usable reply, and both joint replies supported both forecasts. [Control and stop rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:333) · [Tally](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/REREAD2-TALLY.json:77)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **Minor — Add `estimated` to the existing list.** The instructions tell the writer to preserve the qualifier beside the number, but the allowed list could only represent this quote as unqualified. The readers and adjudicators saw the description without the list. I found one affected figure among 251 source figures across the three original writer runs. In memory, adding `estimated` let the corrected F11 pass and left its forecast unchanged. The check rejected both dropping the word and adding it to a quote that lacked it. Disabling the qualifier comparison let the dropped word through. Show readers the same allowed values so they can judge what writers could express. Narrowing the description alone would leave “an estimated $750 billion” recorded as unqualified. [Stored F11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/answers/claude.json:193) · [Schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:110) · [Number check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:487) · [Reader packet builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_rules.py:47)\n     6\t\n     7\t3. **Serious — S is the priority, and the same weakness appears in E.** Both S writers stated their deductions as D741 requires. Zacks gives total spending for the four companies, the $730 billion figure covers AI infrastructure, and NVIDIA’s nearly $800 billion covers five companies. Those figures suggest data centers account for a large share. They do not justify 90% or a 95% floor for the four companies in the question. T10 also uses Zacks’s total as the market reference for data-center spending, a separate scope error already noted in round 57. In E, both readers rejected the 85% share applied to the $20 billion base. That assumption turns a $40 billion comparison into a $34 billion forecast and changes its band. [D741 ruling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11353) · [T10 adjudications](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread2-adjudication/T10.claude.json:3) · [Round 57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r57.md:7) · [E calculation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/E/answers/codex.json:75)\n     8\t\n     9\t4. **Minor — The five controls passed the checks they were built for.** The overlap control tested whether readers recognized a valid range, and those readers still split on whether its forecast was supported. First readers were explicitly asked to name the evidence for the assumption that decides the band. Adjudicators got the broader definition of support without that instruction. T10 shows why this matters. Both adjudicators could check the arithmetic, but they disagreed on whether the sources justified the 95% floor. [Overlap tally](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/REREAD2-TALLY.json:12) · [Reader instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread2.py:22) · [Adjudicator instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_adjudicate.py:24)\n    10\t\n    11\t5. **Recommendation — After Council B agrees, ask Alex to authorize one targeted $0 test.** Prove the qualifier repair on saved replies. Then test a short clarification of the existing instruction: when a deduction decides the band, show what evidence supports its size or a bound that justifies the chosen band. Leave the forecast unresolved if neither is available. Use S and one stored case where the passages do support deriving a narrower figure. Option (a) would mostly sample fresh writers against the same known weakness. Option (b) would require Alex to explicitly change the registered sequence, which sends a clean result to him for the paid request. I verified that S can be shown as unresolved, but that supplies no supported forecast for the current test. If Alex wants a justified unresolved answer to count, register that before a new test. The 36 requests remain the measurement of gpt-6-luna. [Existing unresolved instruction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/S/system.txt:9) · [Usability and paid sequence](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:263) · [D725 paid test](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md:86)\n    12\t\n    13\t   **Falsifier.** The clarification fails if a fresh S answer still picks a band using an unsupported share, or if it withholds the forecast in the case with adequate evidence. Both readers should be able to point to the passage that decides which outcome is warranted.\n    14\t\n    15\tThe review and replays were read-only.     1\t# Round 59, Claude's own reflection (written before reading Codex's)\n     2\t\n     3\t- **The verdict.** STOP on two lines.\n     4\t  - The F11 mark is a format gap. The qualifier enum lacks \"estimated\", while the description invites recording any qualifier the\n     5\t    quote writes. The adjudicators followed the description.\n     6\t  - S has zero usable replies. That is substance: neither writer can support a precise data-center share of total capex from these\n     7\t    passages.\n     8\t- **What the goal needs.** The blind test was built to check that the request states its rules, that the checker is right, and that\n     9\t  readers can tell format from substance. All three now hold:\n    10\t  - the writers have been clean since run 3;\n    11\t  - the checker has had no error since D742;\n    12\t  - the readers pass five controls.\n    13\t  What remains is a model-judgement weakness on one question type, plus a one-word format gap. More $0 rounds on the same writers\n    14\t  re-measure that weakness. They do not change what the paid run would measure in gpt-6-luna.\n    15\t- **My lean: (b).** Close the qualifier gap at its owner: the description says only listed qualifiers are recorded, or \"estimated\"\n    16\t  is added to the list (council to choose), with a case and a mutant. Then take Alex the paid re-send request, with the record of four\n    17\t  readings and the S weakness registered as what the paid run must measure. The registered \"clean result\" bar was not met, so this is\n    18\t  Alex's call, not ours.\n    19\t- **The alternative (c).** A request change: when the passages do not size a deduction, give a bound the passages support, or\n    20\t  answer unresolved. That is a behaviour change. It would need its own test, and it touches ruling 3. It goes to Alex as an option,\n    21\t  not as something I start.\n    22\t- **What I will not do:** run another reading round without a question it can still answer.\n     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging the current rungs of a family of related number theses: one company's quantities that overlap, such as a total and its segment, a level and its growth, or a later year that rests on an earlier year's base. Use only the supplied evidence and themes in force. Each rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Judge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force, as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\n     4\t- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate whose pace you forecast, informed by guidance, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- \"Themes in force\" lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on a member and report it in that member's theme_pushes with the direction it pushes that member (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \"updated since this thesis was last judged\" may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- Your conclusions must be consistent with each other and with the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open.\n     9\t- Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge rather than read or compute is an estimate, stated as yours. When the evidence cannot support a member's forecast, answer it unresolved and say why. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '163,210p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; tail -n 18 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md; sed -n '292,388p' AGENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n| 24 | 11-04 夜 | 第二处：资本开支题的说明加\"资本开支也等于同期经营现金流减自由现金流（按通常的定义）\"；两轮独立复核后补到 14 篇、门槛写死；冻结后发 84 次（0.148 美元） | 没过：现金流那句原样 0/3 没写，加一句后只写了 1/3（且一句话里写出推算的 17 亿）；B–D 没触发；F 失败——一篇 Vera CPU 文章里加一句后三次都改写引用被拒、Perplexity 两次挂到总收入题（与资本开支无关，请求一变整段输出跟着变）。**根子**：营业利润率那句（i163）和现金流那句（i131）在冻结的抽取金标里都是\"已签版 excluded（§5.3 已知事实的重述）、待批第 6 条 optional\"；冻结提示词的复核也教模型\"重述的老情况是杂音\"；而读者 B 判这两道题正是拿它们当现状起点。窗口在五月财报之后才开始，账本里没有更早的记录——冷启动缺口。不是挂题或引用的问题 | 交 Alex：覆盖开始时公司最近一期已公布的数从哪来（第 6 条提议，或覆盖开始时一次性记下基线）；两处小改动都停 |\n| 25 | 11-05 凌晨 | Alex：\"乙\"（D363）：开始跟踪时从公司最近一期财报一次性记下每道题的起点数 | 找到的材料：5 月 20 日的第一季度 8-K 附件 99.1 新闻稿；清洗后的文字丢了财务表，原始网页文字（20,790 字符）里有营业利润（会计准则 535.36 亿、调整后 537.83 亿）、购置固定资产 17.57 亿、经营现金流 503.44 亿、自由现金流 485.54 亿；10-Q 原始文字也有（营业利润占收入 65.6%）但长且杂。最简单的验证：不改任何提示词，把新闻稿当开始跟踪时的第一份材料交给冻结的抽取，3 次；再拿系统自己写下的起点数搭窗口末的判断请求 | 第一步请求已搭好读过；独立读者检查中 |\n| 26 | 11-05 凌晨 | 乙的第一步：新闻稿（带表格的原始文字）交给冻结的抽取当开始跟踪时的第一份材料，3 次；独立读者先查过，把\"怎么算过\"改严（数字必须在存下的引用里、并写明是一季度） | 没过：写下 13–21 条（收入、毛利率、每股收益、指引……挂 v1/v2/v3/v11/v7/v8），**营业利润和购置固定资产两行三次都没写**；冻结的抽取只读新闻稿的文字段落、不读后面的财务表格。第二步拿不到起点数，不做 | 在这一步修：每道题单独问一次财报要它自己的起点数（一次只想一道题），原文那行由代码核对，再走冻结的判断 |\n| 27 | 11-05 凌晨 | 乙的第一步第二版：每道题单独读一次新闻稿要起点数（不改冻结提示词，判断那一步的模型设置）；独立读者先查出四处（例子正是两道题的定义、数字比对太松太严、读错列规则误伤、第二版没写下），核实后照改，25 个对照全对、两个故意弄坏的版本都被抓出 | v10 2/3（第 3 次整行照抄被拒，数是对的）、v12 3/3（自己认出资本开支就是\"购置固定资产和无形资产\"那行）；对照 v4 白卷 3/3；对照 v7 照登记没过——2/3 次交回不是数的说明，其中一条因产品名\"A5X\"里的\"5\"被代码收下；修了数字认法，存下的回答重跑只有这两条变成拒收 | 第二步 |\n| 28 | 11-05 凌晨 | 乙的第二步：只用系统自己读到的数，搭 7 月 14 日的冻结判断请求，v10 两份、v12 三份各发一次，按冻结尺子的规则打分 | **v10 判第 2 档 2/2（算上没判的那次 2/3），v12 判第 4 档 3/3，全在读者 B 的范围里**；理由都是用读到的数算的（65.9%；17.57 亿推全年 50–80 亿）。两步合计约 2.5 美分 | 独立读者核对理由、挑战建议；然后报 Alex |\n| 29 | 11-05 凌晨 | 独立读者核对结果、挑战\"直接做进生产再跑 14 天\"的建议 | 判断理由站得住、记录如实（发之前的版本已还原、锁定码对上）；但只测了 2/22 道题，财报里有挨着但不是那个量的数（v20、v9 旁边），而冻结版本已判对 15–16 道；文件是人挑的；\"和存档比\"违反 PRD 10 | 建议撤回；下一步：同样的读法用在全部 22 道种子题，读到数的题在窗口末判断、当天重发对照，已判对的题一道不能变错 |\n| 30 | 11-05 | Alex：\"你充分验证\"。乙的全部 22 道题验证：设计（`baseline-design.md` 第 8 轮）——文件由代码选（开始跟踪前最近一个财报日的财报类材料：5 月 20 日新闻稿和 CFO 说明）；读法和第二版一字不差，每题每份文件 3 次；判断照 PRD 10 §4 当天原样重发：三遍各自拿窗口末最后一次判断的存档请求，对照原样 3 次，起点组只在证据块最前面加上读到的数；过关三条事先写下（v10、v12 各 ≥ 6/9；不弄坏：同一遍里重排的精确检验显著少、或少 2 次以上且两人读理由认定是起点数带偏；读到的数五类分类，读错、别的量、不是数一个都不能有） | 发之前修了两处：读法的检查原来要求\"引用的最后一个数就是读到的数\"，照抄整句的正常引用会被拒（4 句全拒），改成\"读到的数印在引用里\"（对照 32 例全对，两个弄坏的版本分别抓出 5、1 个错；试点重放只有 v10 第 3 次那两条整行变成收下，v10 变 3/3）；发送脚本按冻结尺子补上是非题判法、\"档动了\"对着请求里那次上一次结论查（三遍存档 57 个结论和 `score_judgement.py` 逐题一致，弄坏的判法被抓出）。审查：Codex 4 轮（第 1 轮 5 条严重、第 2 轮 3 条严重，都属实都改；第 3、4 轮无严重问题），独立读者 1 次（请求干净、没有金标泄漏；挪档看不见、单位后缀、口径错等照改） | 设计和 8 个脚本锁定（`baseline-all.sha256`）；发读数 132 次 |\n| 31 | 11-05 | 乙的全部 22 道题验证，照锁定的设计测一次：读 132 次（0.083 美元）、两人分类（第二位盲分）、判断 144 次（0.344 美元），三遍各自和当天原样重发的对照比 | **第 1 条过**：v10、v12 各 9/9 判对。**第 2 条过**：读到数的 7 道判过的题两组选档逐次一样，只有 v22 第 2 遍少 1 次（7/9 对 6/9，理由显示是本来的抽样起伏，起点组写明\"没有把一季度乘 4\"）。**第 3 条没过**：53 个收下的数里 5 个是别的量——v19（Vera CPU 收入）两次收了\"数据中心计算收入 604 亿\"，v20（Blackwell 和 Rubin 收入）两次收了\"数据中心收入 752 亿\"和\"网络收入 148 亿\"；判断都没被带偏（v19 理由写明计算收入里没有单列 Vera CPU） | 照登记停，交 Alex |\n| 32 | 11-05 | 问模型自己为什么收那 5 个数（3 次，约 0.3 美分，`probe-baseline-account.md`） | 3 次都指向读法任务里那一句\"报告没用题目的名字写这个量时，写出组成它的行、或报告记它的那一行\"，并自己说这些数不是这道题的量、不该写。这一句是 v10、v12 要用的，在报告根本没有这个量的题上把模型推去写更大或旁边的行 | 建议：只改这一句的边界（只收\"由它算出的那几行\"和\"换了名字的同一个量\"，更大的、旁边的行不算），按提示词审计改，再在 22 道题上测一次；等 Alex 的话 |\n| 33 | 11-05 | Alex：\"改\"。只改读法里那一句：原句\"写出组成它的行、或报告记它的那一行\"→ 新句\"只写算出它的那几行，或换了名字的同一个量；更大的行、旁边的行都不写\"（任务 790 → 889 字符，理由：抽象说法换成闭合两类加边界）。提示词审计、Codex 只读审 1 轮（1 条严重：发送失败会被当成白卷，已改成\"不完整、不下结论\"）；先在 v19、v20、v10、v12 上试发 24 次（1.6 美分） | 试发过：v19、v20 三次都白卷，v10 3/3；v12 2/3——问模型（2 次）：新句的\"更大的行\"半句让它把\"购置固定资产和无形资产\"当成比资本开支宽的一行，其中一次重想后改口\"就是资本开支\" | 照登记测全部 22 道题 |\n| 34 | 11-05 | 第三版的登记测试：和第 8 轮一样，只换这一句；读 132 次（0.078 美元）、两人分类（第二位盲分）、读到数的 7 道题三遍重判、当天对照（108 次，0.268 美元） | **三条全过**：v10、v12 各 9/9；判对的题一道没变错（只有 v22 第 2 遍反过来对照 0/3、起点组 3/3，理由是在 41% 和 32% 两个增长估计间摇摆，和第 13 轮方向相反，与起点数无关）；46 个数全是自己的量（2 条是标明的二季度指引），两人分类全一致；v19、v20 的错数全没了，其余 15 道白卷、没冒出新错。没盖住：资本开支那一行试发时漏过 1 次；指引也被写成\"事实\"；一路判下来的效果和跨题效果要端到端才量得到 | 交 Alex：要不要做进生产、跑 14 天三遍端到端 |\n| 35 | 11-05 | 独立读者挑战\"现在做进生产、跑 14 天三遍\"的建议 | 核实属实的：资本开支那一行在新句子下 12 次读漏 3 次（旧句子 9/9，模型两次都怪\"更大的行\"半句）；句子照 5 月财报改、又只在 5 月财报上量，没有留出的财报；做进生产前的记录写法（同一个数挂几道题、指引不该写成\"事实\"、第二个提示词）要 Alex 定；分类和判断同时跑、说明里还引着旧句子，照实记下 | 建议撤回；下一步：修掉资本开支漏读（改成\"写完逐条复核\"），在 5 月和留出的 8 月两份财报上各测一遍，约 0.5 美元 |\n| 36 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好开始做到production 上，完整的更新所有系统设计等\"；同一个数挂几道题，他选\"存一条，挂到每道读到它的题\"（D364）。做进生产前先修资本开支漏读：第四版把\"是不是这道题的量\"挪到最后逐条复核（并删掉别的期间），文件规则补\"有申报的只读申报的\"；Codex 审 3 轮（共 6 条严重，都改）；试发 7 道题过；然后 5 月登记读法、8 月留出读法 | **没过**：5 月\"不能删掉该留的\"——v22 只留住 1/3、资本开支 3/6 读；8 月资本开支二季度 0/3（选了上半年、引用跳格被拒）。机理：复核里\"别的期间删掉\"让全年题删掉最近一季；\"最近一期\"在本季和年初至今两栏间没说清。好消息：8 月 v9 找到了新披露的担保 1,085 亿和承诺 560 亿 | 停，交 Alex：第三版是唯一过了 5 月三条的版本 |\n| 37 | 11-05 | Alex：\"为什么没过？…你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\"；\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\"。普查全部 7 次读法、606 次文件读（`census_all_reads.py`，$0） | 第三版 0 个错数、156 次读漏 3 次（全是资本开支）；第二版 2 个错数；第四版漏 24 次（5 月）、16 次（8 月）。我自己判错的：6 个对的数被我的引用检查拒（漏星号、跳格），8 月\"只认本季\"规则错，第 13 轮 3 条\"有争议\"的数是标准答案自己用的行，第三版全过后又改第四版 | 收敛方案：提示词定为第三版不再改；修引用检查（$0 重放全部 606 次读核对）；在 8 月财报上用第三版读一次（约 8 美分，只有\"收错数\"能叫停）；然后做进生产 |\n| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\"自己的量，别的期间\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n### 7.2 Reading results\n\n- **A score is a lead; the traces are the measurement.** Every measurement has a score, and every time you read the traces yourself: the\n  raw answer beside the article for every missed helpful entry, and a sample of the extras and of the hits; historical gold keeps its original labels. The scorer\n  hard-codes no rule of the standard: it reads the gold file it is given, prints the gold's and the standard's sha256, and refuses a gold\n  made for another version; scores are compared only on the same gold. Do not write a new scorer to judge a probe: read the traces yourself (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n  \"不要写评分器这个之前就出问题过，你自己读trace 来分析\"). Alex, 2026-10-29 (D244): \"我觉得这是最容易出错的问题；你非常容易写死，我们在改的过程中如果drift你会一直用久的标准来衡量，这边需要有打分，但是“一定”要你自己下去看trace这是必须，记起来\".\n- **The ruler counts only what it was built to count.** Before a quality claim, a reader who did not write the change also reads the\n  fields the product stores (original day, original speaker, tier, the summary's hedges) and what the next step does with the record\n  (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"现在到底质量怎么样你深度的解析不要只是看尺子\").\n- Read the judges' reasons, not only the scores, and pick the next fix from the largest cause. Open the samples behind a metric's largest\n  values before reading it, and write down what a derived number reduces to.\n- **Report every number, regressions first.** For future evidence evaluation, combine the existing gold's core and supporting entries as helpful, use its not-kept entries as unhelpful, and leave optional entries neutral (D372). Count one research matter in one article (D250), not raw sentences. Retain the old labels and scores in historical results, and do not silently relabel the frozen gold. One quantity per table column. A comparison of\n  totals uses three draws; a count from one draw is labelled one draw and shows a mechanism, not a difference between arms. Lead with the\n  mechanism and the share of its class it explains, then the fix.\n- **Read what was dropped.** A statement the pipeline drops is thrown away with its reason, never parked on a side list; evaluation\n  reads the dropped statements by hand, classifies them by the mechanism that would have kept them, and fixes the largest class upstream\n  (D209: \"if it doesn't matter, just fucking throw it away … if there are false positives that got thrown away … you got to pick it up\").\n- **Measure end to end before a step's arm, and read the parked designs first.** A step's noise that the next step removes is not the\n  defect, and a step's recall that the next step throws away is. Before any arm on one step: the production replay through the whole path\n  on the gold window, the count at the step the product reads, and the decisions on the topic read for a parked fix (Alex, 2026-10-31:\n  \"make sure we are not going around in circles using wrong ruler and wrong prompts that don't work\"). Before a phase targets one step,\n  the upside of that step done perfectly is measured where the product is judged: the judge is given the gold's own evidence, built by\n  the production code, a few sends (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"我很不开心你的失败，为什么，深度多轮检讨记录，想思路突破\").\n- **Read what was kept against the gold, blind, before the next noise arm.** The not-kept gold entries a version keeps are judged by a\n  reader who wrote neither the gold nor the prompt, mixed with controls it cannot tell apart; where it parts from the gold, the standard\n  is unclear or the gold misreads it, and that goes to Alex before any arm counts it as noise (Alex, 2026-10-31: \"你再次重新检查尺子，看看是不是这些留下的还有歧义；然后再思考怎么降低noise\").\n- Pair every structural check with its semantic one. Run a data rule over its whole input range and on cases it was not tuned on. Weigh\n  a case by what it carries in the product, not by count.\n- A claim about a population (\"the data is clean\") rests on a code sweep of the whole population and an independent read of a fresh\n  random sample, never on the pages the author looked at.\n- Cost is priced from tokens at the published rates (`hivemind.model.PRICES`, cached input at `model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE`), never from a\n  stored `cost_usd`; say which rates a projection uses.\n\n### 7.3 Iterating\n\n- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n  model applies it: before a registered test, the changed request is sent on the cases that motivated it, a few cents.\n- **A failed arm is diagnosed before the next one.** When an arm fixes its class and regresses another, write the root cause first: the\n  process error (what grew, what the small sample did not guard) and the mechanism, traced to the raw answers and the model's account,\n  never a guess stated as the cause. A small sample guards every class the change can move, not only its own. When a fix keeps moving\n  another class, the call is doing several jobs: move the rule to its owner (a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field)\n  rather than add a sentence (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"那你这些修改都是失败的呀，为什么，根因，你要检讨然后再接着尝试。我觉得你已经陷入deep loop 了\").\n  A failed step of a plan is fixed and re-run at that same step: its failures are the work list, and nothing later in the plan and no\n  substitute plan starts before it passes (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"你为什么要drift? 你现在明明还有这么多的问题要fix,你到底知不知道你要fix什么？\").\n  Before a fix is proposed, write which goal the mechanism still serves and what the product already gives for it; a measurement that\n  removes the reason a mechanism exists retires the mechanism instead of starting its repair (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"I told you to think about\n  it and you're giving me suggestions that you reject yourself\").\n- **Before a version is rejected, the rejection is checked.** Every failed or refused answer behind a \"did not pass\" is read against its\n  source and put down as the model's error or the measuring rule's or check's error; a rule or check that refuses right answers is fixed,\n  and a version that already meets the goal (what it was built to fix is fixed, nothing that was right turned wrong) is not dropped for a\n  stricter rule a later review added. Alex, 2026-11-05: \"你到底是不是再搬石头砸自己的脚？各种reject自己，你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\";\n  \"你不能每次都这样判错然后浪费我时间，我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\".\n- **Correct, then cheap.** Make the pipeline right and stable before any cost, speed or throughput work; report cost as a baseline only\n  (Alex, 2026-10-25).\n\n## 8. Product thinking\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'd=docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers; wc -l \"$d/SMALL-DESIGN.md\" \"$d/blind_test.py\" \"$d/blind_reread2.py\" \"$d/blind_adjudicate.py\"; rg -n '\"'D745|\"'^## |P-v8|discount|unsupported|targeted|stop'\"' \\\"\"'$d/SMALL-DESIGN.md\" \"$d/BLIND3-RESULT.md\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'd=docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers; wc -l \"$d/SMALL-DESIGN.md\" \"$d/blind_test.py\" \"$d/blind_reread2.py\" \"$d/blind_adjudicate.py\"; rg -n '\"'D745|\"'^## |P-v8|discount|unsupported|targeted|stop'\"' \\\"\"'$d/SMALL-DESIGN.md\" \"$d/BLIND3-RESULT.md\"'","aggregated_output":"     348 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md\n     219 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py\n     119 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread2.py\n     121 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_adjudicate.py\n     807 total\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:19:## 1. What is dropped, and where it goes\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:32:## 2. The rules code enforces (revised after round 52, `codex-r52.md`; the revision is marked [52])\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:59:## 2-old. The rules as first written (superseded by the revision above)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:78:## 3. The wire schema, word for word (examples from no covered company, AGENTS §6)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:143:## 4. Build\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:162:## 5. The $0 blind test (registered; REPAIR-DESIGN.md §5 with rounds 51's fixes)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:168:| P (joint), P-v4, P-v8 (separate) | old-1 v4 8810, v8 8816 | NVIDIA revenue company FY2027; NVIDIA revenue Data Center FY2027 | 431.2/392/352.8/313.6; 400/350/300/250 | the pair; 79 quotes absent from the gate |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:252:- **An accepted reply with a named defect** (marked by both readers, or by the third reader) is a stop.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:267:**Stop.** The test stops on any of these:\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:279:**[D742] Registered before the third run (council rounds 56–56c).** The re-run stopped on one S4 refusal of a sound answer\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:285:- **The stop lines are unchanged.**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:289:  A sound answer refused under a clearly stated condition still stops the run.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:295:  - A settled defect on an accepted reply is a stop.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:296:  - A split is disclosed, not a stop.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:320:  - The registered stop lines apply to the 12 replies exactly as before, with adjudication where the readers disagree.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:322:  - Any registered stop on the 12 replies, including S losing its only usable reply, sends the result back to council.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:341:  | K-unsupported | E's Claude reply, 140% growth that its own reasons argue against | supported = no |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:344:  - The registered stop lines apply to the 12 replies as before, with adjudication where readers disagree. The adjudication packet now\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:346:  - Any failed control or any registered stop ends the re-read, and the result goes back to council.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:24:## 1. Writers' first answers (`CHECKED.json`)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:30:| P-v8 | 387.4, rung 2 | 388.1, rung 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:35:## 2. Readers and adjudicators (`TALLY.json`)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:51:  This is not a registered stop line (usable is counted per case, and S has R01). It is a real judgement error in an answer that would\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:57:## 3. What the test shows\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:62:- **The stop this time is in the measuring instrument.** The reader brief's definition is narrower than the format the writer was\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:64:- **The readers did their job on substance.** They found the one reply whose decisive assumption is unsupported (R07). That is the\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:74:  - R07's unsupported share.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:76:## 4. The blinded re-read (D743, Alex: \"补上那条，重读一遍\"; `reread-packets/`, `reread-adjudication/`, `REREAD-TALLY.json`)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:84:- **STOP again, as written: Q10 (P-v8, Codex writer).**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:90:  adjudication packet carries them and its definitions say \"allowing what the format rules permit\". Both stops caused by the instrument\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:102:## 5. The second blinded re-read (D744, Alex: \"批准再重读一次\"; `reread2-packets/`, `reread2-adjudication/`, `REREAD2-TALLY.json`)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:108:    marked by both; K-unsupported was \"not supported\" by both.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md:134:  | P-v8 | both writers |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
