{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"d=docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers; rg -n 'unresolved|def publish_decision|def from_answer' \\\"\"'$d/calc_small.py\" \"$d/render_v13.py\" \"$d/paid_gate.py\"; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '\"'11342,11369p'; rg -n 'D725|discounted by default' docs/DECISIONS-log.md \\\"\"'$d/RESULT.md\" \"$d/REQUEST-AUDIT.md\"'","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:67:        'shape': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['forecast', 'unresolved']},\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:130:                            \"none for an unresolved one. Its what is the member's outcome key, in USD bn.\"),\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:141:        'shape': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['forecast', 'unresolved'], 'description': 'forecast: a figure marked in outcome_for, a rung, and '\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:142:                  'a reference (a figure marked in reference_for, or reference_unavailable). unresolved: why; rung and reference_unavailable '\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:11:refusal makes the unit unresolved. The separate arm's two answers are then reconciled by the same checks over the pair's family.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:282:    attempt (a second refusal is unresolved). A unit with no started line is not sent; one started but not finished is interrupted.\"\"\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:301:            if decision == 'refused':                          # a second refusal is unresolved; a first with no retry sent is incomplete\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:302:                decision = 'unresolved' if len(done) >= 2 else 'retry not sent'\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:466:             'deciding_gap': 'an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band'}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:160:def from_answer(data, family):\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:186:        if a.get('shape') == 'unresolved':\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:188:                errors.append(('S7', f'{v}: an unresolved answer has why, rung and reference_unavailable null, and no figure marked for it'))\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:556:        if member is None or a.get('shape') == 'unresolved':\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:782:def publish_decision(family, calc, result):\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:783:    \"\"\"'refused' when a check fails; 'held' when a member is unresolved and a declared relation joins it to another member; else\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:784:    'publish' (an unresolved member is shown as unresolved).\"\"\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:787:    unresolved = {a['view_id'] for a in calc['answers'] if a.get('shape') == 'unresolved'}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:790:        if ends & unresolved and ends - unresolved:\n 11342\t    - apply the rulings, in the reader brief and in code only where the structure decides them;\n 11343\t    - verify both reader families on the stored boundary replies;\n 11344\t    - re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers, then the paid re-send request.\n 11345\t\n 11346\t## D741 · 2026-11-22 · Alex rules the three reader questions of D740\n 11347\t\n 11348\t- **The questions** (after D740), each with its options; the recommended option is listed first:\n 11349\t  - 【增速参考】\"写手用公司指引的三季度 1080 亿算出“指引隐含增速约 12%”，参考它定四季度增速 13%，再套在自己预测的三季度 1136 亿上。进入收入计算的三季度数只有 1136 亿这一个。这算不算“同一季度用了两个数”的错？\" Options: 不算错 (推荐); 算错.\n 11350\t  - 【市场参照】\"分析师预期公司全年总收入 4110 亿，最近一个季度数据中心占 92.5%，乘出来约 3800 亿。能不能把这 3800 亿叫作“市场对数据中心全年的预期”？\" Options: 不能 (推荐); 能.\n 11351\t  - 【总开支当数据中心开支】\"问题问四大云厂商“数据中心资本开支”，原文只给了“总资本开支”（并说大部分投向 AI 基础设施）。一份答案直接拿总开支当数据中心开支，没扣非数据中心的部分。可以吗？\" Options: 必须写明扣多少 (推荐); 可以直接用.\n 11352\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"不算错 (推荐)\"; \"不能 (推荐)\"; \"必须写明扣多少 (推荐)\".\n 11353\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11354\t  1. **Not a defect:** a growth rate computed from guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate, when one figure\n 11355\t     supplies the quarter in the revenue calculation.\n 11356\t  2. **Not the market's reference:** consensus for a total × a past quarter's reported share. That figure is our comparison estimate.\n 11357\t     Only an outside figure for the member's own quantity (for example Morningstar's direct segment estimate), or a calculation that\n 11358\t     carries no past period's reported share or multiple to another period, is the market's reference.\n 11359\t  3. **A total used for a narrower quantity** (total capex for data-center capex) must state the deduction as its own figure, or give\n 11360\t     a supported bound that shows where the narrower quantity lands.\n 11361\t- **How they are applied (D738):**\n 11362\t  - Ruling 2's carried share is structural, so S5 refuses it.\n 11363\t  - Rulings 1 and 3 go in the request and in the reader brief, because they turn on what a label or an estimate means.\n 11364\t  - Then three steps:\n 11365\t    1. fix the S1 \"from … to …\" range (D740);\n 11366\t    2. check that both reader families apply the rulings the same way to the stored boundary replies;\n 11367\t    3. re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers.\n 11368\t\n 11369\t## D742 · 2026-11-22 · The v13s re-run stops on one sound answer refused by S4; council 56–56c keeps S4 and makes the request state one benchmark rule; a third $0 blind run follows\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10957:## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10993:- **The questions** (after D725):\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11001:  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11067:- **Not shown:** how a model uses the format (the paid gate, D725), production lifecycle, the product request builder.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11080:- **Decided (Alex):** the sender and the blind reading packets for D725's paid gate are built, rehearsed at $0 and reviewed by the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11090:- **Decided by the council (D725's lines unchanged):**\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11091:  - The first attempt is scored on both arms. D725 registers the arms \"under the same format and checks\" and says nothing about\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11126:- **Registered result (D725's lines, scored as written, D680):** all 72 answers refused by `calc_check.py`, none published; the joint\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11129:- **What it measures:** not D725's question (whether one call over a family gives better numbers), only that the answer format, as\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11163:    - Only then is a re-send of the same 36 requests asked for, under a new decision with D725's lines unchanged.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11180:  - A clean result goes back to Alex as a request to re-send the same 36 requests under a new decision, with D725's lines\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11194:  - Codex answered that the six drop C8's guard against adding a segment into its total, a defect D725 named. Shrinking changes the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11255:    D725's lines.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11501:  - Claude agrees: the weakness is unsupported precision in a number that decides the rung, which is the goal's own failure (D725).\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REQUEST-AUDIT.md:10:| L1 \"judging a thesis's current rung … Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes\" | \"the current rungs of a family of related number theses …\"; dependency conclusions removed | D725 (the unit is a family); the family has no dependency reads |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REQUEST-AUDIT.md:21:| L10 the output list (one rung, reference, implied_outcome …) | \"Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge … is an estimate, stated as yours. When the evidence cannot support a member's forecast, answer it unresolved …\" | D725, DESIGN §2; field definitions moved to the schema |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REQUEST-AUDIT.md:26:- The only new rules are the three D725 contracts: one calculation, figures labelled, and unresolved allowed. Code enforces each.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/REQUEST-AUDIT.md:27:- The product-target sentence (\"discounted by default\") is kept. D721 and Codex's round 43 found that the gold relies on it (q19).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
